            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of temporary sequential atrioventricular electrocardiostimulation on hemodynamics].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A comparative study of the hemodynamic parameters in 22 patients with coronary heart disease and chronic atrioventricular block, Stage II and III, showed a favourable hemodynamic effect of atrioventricular versus ventricular electrocardiostimulation. Tests with isometric and nitroglycerin loads may be used to identify patients in the most urgent need for atrioventricular electrocardiostimulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
